#TODO: Update the unit test with new Scenario
Feature: Read Resource Type

  Background:
    Given a Resource Type for API key '22ee17bd-699e-4b6b-a30b-e854e6c57552' with specific attributes exists
      """json
      {
         "key": "FAQ-R",
         "name": "FAQ-R",
         "description": "Frequently Asked Question Project 1",
         "actions": [
            "view",
            "update",
            "create",
            "delete"
         ]
      }
      """
    And a Resource Type for API key '22ee17bd-699e-4b6b-a30b-e854e6c57552' with specific attributes exists
      """json
        {
           "key": "FAQ-S",
           "name": "FAQ-S",
           "description": "Frequently Asked Question Project 1",
           "actions": [
              "view",
              "update",
              "create",
              "delete"
           ],
           "tags": [
              "tag1",
              "tag2"
           ]
        }
      """

  Scenario: Success: Get All Resource Types
    Given The Resource Admin wants to get All Resource Type with API key '22ee17bd-699e-4b6b-a30b-e854e6c57552'
    When the Resource Admin requests to get all Resource Type
    Then the request is successfully with response code 200
    And a list of all Resource Type is returned in the response
      """json
      {
         "results": [
            {
               "key": "FAQ-R",
               "name": "FAQ-R",
               "description": "Frequently Asked Question Project 1",
               "actions": [
                  "view",
                  "update",
                  "create",
                  "delete"
               ],
               "tags": null
            },
            {
               "key": "FAQ-S",
               "name": "FAQ-S",
               "description": "Frequently Asked Question Project 1",
               "actions": [
                  "view",
                  "update",
                  "create",
                  "delete"
               ],
               "tags": [
                  "tag1",
                  "tag2"
               ]
            }
         ],
         "metadata": {
            "totalCount": 1,
            "totalPageCount": 1,
            "size": 10
         }
      }
      """

  Scenario: Success: Get All Resource Types with Search by name and keyword
    Given The Resource Admin wants to get All Resource Type with API key '22ee17bd-699e-4b6b-a30b-e854e6c57552'
    When the Resource Admin requests to get all Resource Type with type 'name' and keyword 'FAQ-S'
    Then the request is successfully with response code 200
    And a list of all Resource Type is returned in the response
      """json
      {
         "results": [
            {
               "key": "FAQ-S",
               "name": "FAQ-S",
               "description": "Frequently Asked Question Project 1",
               "actions": [
                  "view",
                  "update",
                  "create",
                  "delete"
               ],
               "tags": [
                  "tag1",
                  "tag2"
               ]
            }
         ],
         "metadata": {
            "totalCount": 1,
            "totalPageCount": 1,
            "size": 10
         }
      }
      """

  Scenario: Negative: Get All Resource Types with Search by wrong type and keyword
    Given The Resource Admin wants to get All Resource Type with API key '22ee17bd-699e-4b6b-a30b-e854e6c57552'
    When the Resource Admin requests to get all Resource Type with type 'segment' and keyword 'FAQ-S'
    Then the request is fails with response code 404
    Then the response body read includes status 404 and error message 'Not Found'

  Scenario: Success: Get Resource Type by key
    Given Resource Admin wants to retrieve a Resource Type with the key 'FAQ-R' and API key '22ee17bd-699e-4b6b-a30b-e854e6c57552'
    When the Resource Admin requests to get Resource Type by key
    Then the request is successfully with response code 200
    And return the resource type
      """
      {
         "key": "FAQ-R",
         "name": "FAQ-R",
         "description": "Frequently Asked Question Project 1",
         "actions": [
            "view",
            "update",
            "create",
            "delete"
         ],
         "tags": null
      }
      """

  Scenario: Success: Get Resource Type by key that has tags
    Given Resource Admin wants to retrieve a Resource Type with the key 'FAQ-S' and API key '22ee17bd-699e-4b6b-a30b-e854e6c57552'
    When the Resource Admin requests to get Resource Type by key
    Then the request is successfully with response code 200
    And return the resource type
      """
      {
         "key": "FAQ-S",
         "name": "FAQ-S",
         "description": "Frequently Asked Question Project 1",
         "actions": [
            "view",
            "update",
            "create",
            "delete"
         ],
         "tags": [
            "tag1",
            "tag2"
         ]
      }
      """

  Scenario: Success: Get Resource Type with an existing/duplicate key but with different project
    Given a Resource Type for API key '22ee17bd-699e-4b6b-a30b-e854e6c57722' with specific attributes exists
      """json
      {
         "key": "FAQ-R",
         "name": "FAQ-R",
         "description": "Frequently Asked Question Project 2",
         "actions": [
            "view",
            "update",
            "create",
            "delete"
         ]
      }
      """
    And Resource Admin wants to retrieve a Resource Type with the key 'FAQ-R' and API key '22ee17bd-699e-4b6b-a30b-e854e6c57722'
    When the Resource Admin requests to get Resource Type by key
    Then the request is successfully with response code 200
    And return the resource type
      """json
      {
         "key": "FAQ-R",
         "name": "FAQ-R",
         "description": "Frequently Asked Question Project 2",
         "actions": [
            "view",
            "update",
            "create",
            "delete"
         ],
         "roles": null
      }
      """

  Scenario: Negative Get Resource Type by a non-existent Key
    Given Resource Admin wants to retrieve a Resource Type with the key "wrong_key" and API key '22ee17bd-699e-4b6b-a30b-e854e6c57552'
    When the Resource Admin requests to get Resource Type by key
    Then the request is fails with response code 404
    Then the response body read includes status 404 and error message 'Not Found'
